    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAll attempts to enter insert mode (i) in a terminal buffer currently get redirected to terminal mode (t). The terminal buffer can already be modified with normal mode commands by setting 'modifiable'. It would make sense to be able to modify it in insert mode as well.  This would also make attempts at solving #23645 much simpler and smoother feeling, as the command area of the buffer could be edited without sending inputs to the terminal process.\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAdd a way to force enter insert mode in terminal buffers. No changes to existing behaviour. Maybe:\n- API only: `nvim__term_start_insert`\n- Command: `:startinsert!` is already taken, maybe `startinsert ++force` \n\n### How\n\nMinimal: add a flag for going to insert mode that bypasses the current terminal mode interception.\nMaybe better: Separate the logic for entering terminal mode from the logic for entering insert mode, rather than mixing both like in the current implementation.\n\n### Cost\n\nSince terminal buffers are already modifiable, I think the cost is low. ",
